okay so we finally got to see the rings  of the mandarin  in the new shang chi trailer and it's  kind of cool right we're gonna break  this whole thing down here which is  gonna be kind of tough to do because  honestly the trailer didn't really give  us anything that we hadn't seen in the  first one but there were a few big  things that we saw  number one we finally know where emil  blonsky's been right abomination was  like in the great big huge fighting cage  not really sure how he escaped last i  heard last i saw if i remember correctly  and it's been a long time since i saw  the incredible hulk with edward norton i  guess he was just let loose  anyway regardless of the situation  that's where he is now which is kind of  cool to see them actually do something  with emil blonsky by god i never thought  he was going to make his return  the second thing that we got to see is  what looked like finn fang foom now  supposedly the idea of fin fang fume  in chiang chi had been completely  debunked like three weeks ago  so only one of two things is going on  either it was being debunked because  they were lying to us and they just  wanted to build up the hype and  excitement so that when it was revealed  that it was finn fang fume it'd be a  great big huge deal  or that's accident car i'm more inclined  to believe that it's action car just  given the origin of the ten rings and  the mandarin and all that kind of stuff  but it's a giant dragon  fin fang fume is a giant dragon okay so  let's turn to the comments explain for a  second because there's not a whole lot  to break down here i mean it's kind of a  cool trailer  let's give you guys a little bit of  history about the 10 rings the mandarin  what the rings are how all that stuff  works  okay so there was a comic book ron of  iron man that was written by a guy named  matt fraction a  legendary iron man comic book run and i  have it all over comics explained so  make sure you guys check out the  description at the end of this video but  the whole thing behind this is it gave  us a really  more updated and a really really  accurate origin for the mandarin so the  way this worked is that the mandarin was  actually a guy who was born to a  prostitute in an opium den  yeah didn't really come into the world  in the best situation  but ultimately he ended up basically  escaping after his mom died and then he  got caught up in the communist  revolution in china which  ultimately he ended up fleeing china  because he was considered a fugitive now  an invincible iron man issue 522 which  was written by matt fraction we found  out that the mandarin had actually  traveled to a place called the valley of  spirits  where he came across a cave that was  being occupied by axing car  now action car is what you call a  mcluhan that's also the same thing that  finn thing fume is  these are basically extraterrestrial  aliens finn fang boom looks like a giant  dragon he really is in a lot of ways a  giant dragon technically he's a shape  shifter but the form he takes is that of  a giant dragon but axon carr was  basically a mcluhan who left his world  and even his own galaxy to explore the  universe and to see if there was any  other intelligent life there he arrived  on earth and found intelligent life  the problem is the intelligence of the  life on earth led them to kill him  or at least mortally wound him and so  when the mandarin found axon carr  in the cave he killed him and then took  the 10 rings now the 10 rings are  basically these items that were actually  powering the ship in the the original  story but they actually have power of  their own technically they encase the  spirits  of like long dead cosmic warriors and so  a person who possesses the rings  can use the power of the warriors the  idea behind it though is it's very much  like the ring of sauron from lord of the  rings in the sense that when a person is  in possession of the ten rings they have  this constant drive and desire to  actually help those cosmic warriors  return to their normal bodies and that  started to play out to a degree during  matt fraction's run when the mandarin  forced tony stark to build these great  big huge  mech suits that the cosmic warrior  spirits could occupy it didn't quite  work out and i believe that was in the  story called the rings but it didn't  quite work out and so of course you know  the day was more or less saved from the  earth being conquered by  cosmic beings with seemingly unlimited  power  but to break these rings down here's how  they work and here's how these rings  function  so the first ring you have here is one  called the remaker and this basically  allows the mandarin to  alter the molecular structure or the  atomic structure of matter but there are  limitations  it does not allow the mandarin for  example to turn a teacup into  like a pot of gold or something like  that he can't really transmute matter so  he can't turn something into something  else  he can just kind of manipulate the  atomic structure of it this is kind of a  way for marvel to explain  yeah he can use the ring to alter the  atomic structure of matter but he's  never going to be on the same level as  the molotow man owen reese he can't  alter reality on a universal scale  just on a super small scale the second  ring is called  influence and this is basically just a  ring that allows the mandarin to emit  like concussive blast right to literally  just  blast people with huge amounts of energy  now there doesn't really seem to be a  definitive upper limit to the amount of  energy he can use and the energy seems  to be relative to whatever villain  he's facing off against at the time more  often than not marvel's kept it pretty  small  mostly because of the fact that the  mandarin is largely an iron man villain  and so you don't really need the ability  to shatter a world  when you're fighting iron man the third  ring is called spin  and this is one that basically allows  the person who's using it to kind of  emit this vortex to create what is  basically a mini tornado  and they can use this for a couple  different ways one they can encase other  people in it and they can trap them  there  they can throw them off their guard in  the case of iron man he can use it on  him and just make him spin  you can use it to make yourself fly but  it's basically the ability to control  the air around you  and use that for a variety of different  purposes usually it's used with flight  the next one is called nightbringer and  this is actually a ring that's a little  bit wonky here so the whole idea behind  nightbringer is it basically allows the  mandarin to encase a person in what is  more or less living darkness and marvel  comics we call this dark force energy  the dark force dimension is kind of a  weird thing right it's not like the dark  dimension of dormammu  but it's a wholly separate dimension  whereby it's kind of like a ethereal  sort of  substance that actually absorbs light  and so because of that if you encase a  person  in this no light can get in and no light  can get out and they're literally just  wrapped in this this  kind of substance there's no way for  them to escape and so from that point  going forward for however long the  mandarin keeps them encased there  unless a person's able to escape from it  they'll be locked in eternal darkness  they'll never know where they are  like literally they could start walking  in a forward direction and get hit by a  car  it's a weird thing it's cool you don't  really see it all that often  now the funny thing is that this ring  also has a few other caveats to it light  force generations the ability to  basically blind a person with a bright  light  the ability to create magnetic fields  the ability to enhance the gravity  around  individuals so the nightbringer ring is  intriguing in that it's different from a  lot of the other rings because it has a  couple extra caveats that the other  rings simply just don't have  now incandescence is a pretty  straightforward ring this one just  allows him to emit and control  fire not a whole lot to it besides that  now the liar  is my personal favorite ring and this is  the one that allows the mandarin to  manipulate the thoughts of others  but when he uses this he in effect has a  low grade level of what we would call  telepathy throughout marvel comics so  using the liar ring does not put him on  the same scale as like jean grey or  professor x of the x-men there'd be no  way he could overcome them given that  ring but  he is able to use it to create like  mental illusions or to trick people into  believing that an original idea is  actually their own  instead of his it really is just  telepathy in its most pure form now  whenever the mandarin uses the liar ring  one of the things he most commonly does  with it is create mental paralysis and  this does a couple different things  depending on the context and who's  writing the story  either it's straight up paralysis where  the person's mind is completely shut  down and they go into what's effectively  a comatose state or  it keeps the brain from being able to  send messages to the rest of the body  so they are effectively locked inside  their own head again it really depends  on who's writing the story there brian  michael bendis has done it one way  matt fraction is done at another but at  the end of the day it all still pretty  much achieves the same result which is  incapacitating that person using mental  abilities now the last two rings  lightning and zero are a lot like  incandescents they're pretty basic  lightning as you can guess allows the  mandarin to emit and to control  lightning zero allows him to emit and to  control cold now one of the big  differences here with zero and somebody  like iceman bobby drake  is the mandarin's abilities are not on  that same level right iceman bobby drake  is an omega level mutant he has the  ability if he chose to to actually  freeze the core of the earth and kill  life on it the mandarin  doesn't quite have that ability again  his powers are on a much smaller scale  so encasing people in ice making them  incredibly cold freezing the environment  around him that kind of a thing  but again it's all done in a localized  space as opposed to potentially being  done  in a global space but those are the  rings of the mandarin that's basically  how they all work  one of the things that's interesting  about the movie is instead of them being  actual rings that he wears on his  fingers  instead they're bracelets so i don't  know why they don't call it shang chi in  the legends of the tin bracelets  probably because it just doesn't have  the same ring to it right no pun  intended  but it just doesn't quite have the same  kind of you know pizzazz right just  doesn't roll off the tongue as well  which is fine and also if we're looking  at the idea of that dragon which is  hopefully finn fang fume having been the  person that originally wielded the rings  well it would make sense they would have  to be bracelets because that guy's  fingers are probably  huge so he wouldn't have to they would  have to fit on those fingers means those  rings would have to be enormous  but having said that one of the big  things that goes on here and this is  something to kind of keep in mind when  it comes to the movie is we don't  exactly know how those rings  are coming to the mandarin we don't know  if the rings somehow have the caveat of  giving him an extended lifespan  if those rings have been passed down  over the course of generations and the  trailer he says  over the course of my life he doesn't  say over the course of our entire family  history it's just  over the course of my life so we don't  know how far back those go  and if they focus largely on the comics  then it could be one of these things  where the mandarin just stumbled across  the rings in his youth  and has been using them ever since it  may be one of these things where it was  largely given to him  under the pretenses he would use it for  good and then in turn decide to use it  for evil we've seen stuff like that play  out marvel comics all the time  that's how doctor doom stole all the  vibranium and wakanda was by tricking  the panther god baths so this is pretty  common stuff to take place in marvel  comics we see it happen all the time but  again  the marvel cinematic universe kind of  has its own format and its own function  it changes things around a little bit  but  you know the thing about the trailer it  looks like they're obviously keeping a  lot of things hidden right a lot of the  major plot of the movie a lot of the  little easter eggs that we're gonna see  maybe other appearances that are gonna  show up they're keeping a lot of that  stuff contained  this had a lot of recycled footage from  the first trailer  so i'm not too upset about it honestly i  kind of expected that it's only the  second trailer i imagine once we get to  the final trailer the actual  end-all be-all trailer just before the  film's release we'll start getting some  new footage and if we don't  no big deal at least i don't have to  worry about going into the movie and  having it spoiled for me so  with that being said guys let me know  what you think about the trailer down in  the comments section  and we will catch you all later peace
 

